Apple is developing an all-new operating system that is essentially a mix of tvOS, watchOS, and iOS, according to <em>Bloomberg</em>'s Mark Gurman.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/02/iOS-26-Home-Feature.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1034994" /><br/>
In his <a href="https://www.bloomberg.com/news/newsletters/2026-09-20/apple-s-home-ai-hub-details-apple-fitness-layoffs-and-iphone-duo-apple-pencil-mu9vv9k0">latest <em>Power On</em> newsletter</a>, Gurman reiterated that the operating system will feature a grid of app icons, widgets, and customizable clock faces.<br/>
<br/>
The new software platform is intended for <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/21/apple-smart-home-display-coming-next-month/">Apple's long-rumored smart home hub</a>. With built-in facial recognition, Gurman reported that the hub can identify who is looking at the display and show personalized information. As a user approaches the hub, or moves away from it, the size of the interface elements will automatically change.<br/>
<br/>
The operating system could be named homeOS, according to <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/06/05/homeos-trademark-filings/">trademark activity</a> from a shell company that is potentially linked to Apple.<br/>
<br/>
homeOS would join iOS, iPadOS, macOS, watchOS, tvOS, and visionOS.<br/>
<br/>
The hub will essentially combine a HomePod-like speaker with a 6-inch or 7-inch square display. Siri AI is expected to be at the core of the new operating system, and other rumored features include FaceTime video calls, HomeKit accessory management, home security monitoring, photo galleries, a calendar, music playback, and more.<br/>
<br/>
Some of the preinstalled Apple apps that will apparently be available on the new platform include Calendar, Camera, Apple Music, Apple Podcasts, Apple News, Reminders, Notes, and the all-new Siri app for Siri AI conversations.<br/>
<br/>
Finally, the platform will supposedly have multi-user support.<br/>
<br/>
